    "explanation": "Both of you: the GPS trace settles the route question. The trace measures this trip at 7.89 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff, against a platform optimal of 6.20 km — an excess of 1.69 km, or 27.3% of optimal. That passes both of POL-RD-01's establishment tests (more than 0.80 km and more than 20% of optimal), so a route deviation is established. It is well below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gates, so the POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation check is not engaged and there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. The trace is clean — 121 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps — so it fails none of the POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment limbs, needs no independent corroboration, and the burden shift under POL-RD-08 stands on this trace alone.\n\nThe driver's explanation that the road avoided busy junctions is an assertion of an external traffic cause. Tested under POL-RD-13 against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else, it goes nowhere: the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00518-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. No rider-requested detour excuses any part of the excess either — the chat_log is empty (0 messages), so POL-RD-04 fails at its first requirement. No endpoint was amended (POL-RD-05), the fare is METERED rather than an upfront quote (POL-RD-11), and the trip is a RYDE_TAXI with no matched pooled itinerary (POL-RD-12).\n\nThe refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. charged_total = 16.13. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 6.20 + 0.28 x 10.50) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN) + 0.80 platform fee = 12.19, with no ERP, toll, airport surcharge, waiting fee or promo to adjust. Refund = 16.13 - 12.19 = 3.94, rounded up to SGD 3.95. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so it is payable, but at 24.4% of the charge it is far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND. There are no ERP gantries, tolls or surcharges on this fare, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top and its anti-double-count rule is satisfied. The ledger shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00: whatever the app appeared to do when the dispute was pressed, no refund has been recorded, so the SGD 3.95 is money still to be returned. No escalation trigger fires — identifiers and timestamps match across the three instruments, the trace is unimpaired, and the recomputed refund is nowhere near the SGD 150 ceiling.\n\nRider, on the phone call: the trip record shows one call, placed through the app by the DRIVER, answered and lasting 190 seconds, so no private number of yours appears on this record. The ruling values in POL-GEN-03 provide no remedy for driver conduct, and a conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) requires an established repeat pattern, which the driver's profile (0 deviation flags in 90 days, 250 completed trips) does not supply. If the call still concerns you, raise it with in-app support outside this fare dispute. Driver, the deviation is small but real and it is not excused, so the partial refund stands. Confidence 0.90."
