    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation dispute over a fare of SGD 16.13. The GPS trace for the trip is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes: 121 fixes at a 10-second interval, zero gaps, 100% coverage, so it decides the distance question and needs no corroboration. It measures the trip at 7.89 km (the governing figure under POL-RD-01; the trip record's 7.90 km is a rounded convenience copy and is not used for the test) against a platform optimal of 6.20 km. The excess is 1.69 km, or 27.26% of optimal, which passes both establishment tests (greater than 0.80 km and greater than 20%), so a deviation is established. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (under 8.0 km and under 50%) and no repeat-deviation pattern exists on the driver's profile (0 flags in 90 days against 250 completed trips), so no full-refund uplift and no driver-conduct referral follow.\n\nThe driver's explanation that the road was a shortcut when the main road was busy carries no weight. It is an uncited assertion of an external traffic cause; tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else (POL-RD-13), there is no advisory to test it against. EV-ADVIS-00518-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Because no party cited an advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, and it does not send the case to a human reviewer (POL-RD-13(1)); it simply leaves the excess undiminished.\n\nNo other exculpatory clause applies. The chat log is empty, so there is no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04). No endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km is null), so POL-RD-05 does not re-quote the baseline. The fare is METERED, not an upfront quote, so POL-RD-11 is closed, and the vehicle was a RYDE_TAXI with a null solo-optimal figure, so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nThe remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, with the figures on separate lines: charged_total = SGD 16.13; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 6.20 + 0.28 x 10.50) x 1.0, the surge multiplier read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 12.19; refund = 16.13 - 12.19 = SGD 3.94, rounded up to SGD 3.95. There are no ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge to add, so POL-RD-09 neither enlarges nor reduces the figure (and its anti-double-count rule is satisfied). The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis floor and is 24.4% of the fare, below the 90% that would convert it to a full refund. The ruling is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.95.\n\nOn the rider's two remaining points: the recollection that the app 'refunded the difference immediately' is not borne out by the ledger - payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00 - so the charge stands until this refund is issued. The call that now upsets the rider was an in-app platform call placed by the driver, answered and lasting 190 seconds; it exposed no private number of the rider's, none of the ruling values provides a remedy for it, and no conduct referral is available because no repeat-deviation pattern is established. No referral is issued."
